# /workspace and /roadmap are real built HTML entry points (workspace.html,
# roadmap.html — see vite.config.ts), served as static assets by Cloudflare
# Pages just like /privacy and /terms. Each boots the full App, which renders
# the right view from location.pathname.
#
# We deliberately do NOT rewrite them to /index.html here: Cloudflare Pages
# canonicalizes an /index.html destination and bounces the request to `/`,
# which is what sent hard refreshes back to the landing page.

# SPA rewrite for nested section subpaths, so a hard refresh / direct hit on a
# deep URL is served by that section's SPA shell (which then boots the App and
# renders the right view from location.pathname) instead of 404ing.
#
# The destination MUST be the clean, extensionless URL (/roadmap), NOT the .html
# file (/roadmap.html). Cloudflare Pages' Clean URLs canonicalize ANY .html
# destination and 308-redirect it to its extensionless form — so /roadmap.html
# bounces the request to /roadmap, dropping the deep path. The clean URL is
# already canonical, so it is proxied (200) in place with the deep URL preserved.
/blog/*      /blog      200
/roadmap/*   /roadmap   200
